CORE
JmlTrivialGetterKotlin
--function "experiment.JmlTrivialGetterKotlin.validate:(Lexperiment/ColumnAttributes;)V" --jml-source src/main/kotlin/JmlTrivialGetterKotlin.kt --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for chained trivial getters on Kotlin data
classes. JML clauses can call

  attrs.getSensitivity().getViewable()

and JBMC's resolver descends through both Kotlin-emitted
getter methods, recognising each as a trivial field-read
(`return this.sensitivity` then `return this.viewable`),
producing the equivalent member-access chain

  *attrs.sensitivity.viewable

against the backing fields. This is the AWS-Bastion privacy-
pipeline idiom.
